#
# vdc_dma.checks - one row per CHECK of fixtures/src/vdc_dma.s (D-125, plan 04-10). Columns separated by one TAB: check index (1-based), slug, class tag, meaning, and for a raw measurement row a fifth column, the word observe (D-169, F-41).
# Class tags: MAN:<page> (a manual page value; the page label must be in fixtures/lib/cites.txt), GUEST:<model>, ASSUMED:<LED-id>. The transfer count LENR + 1 and the LENR high byte trigger are H7-12, the DCR bits H7-11, the DV rules H7-4; the copy takes time, IW never applies, the overlap rule and the cut at a display start are modelling choices of LED-VID-0014 (VL1: no speed
# is claimed). A pass is not a support claim (ER-4).
id=20
checks=24
1	last-word-not-yet	ASSUMED:LED-VID-0014	Right after the LENR high byte write the last destination word still holds its sentinel: an instant transfer fails this row
2	dst-low-sum	GUEST:vram-sum	The 64 destination low bytes equal an additive running sum, a different computation from the assembler's multiplication that formed the source table: the OR of the differences is zero
3	dst-high-sum	GUEST:vram-sum	The 64 destination high bytes equal the same running sum
4	word-after-block	MAN:H7-12	The word after the block still holds its sentinel: LENR + 1 words moved and not one more
5	lenr0-one-word	MAN:H7-12	LENR = 0 moves one word: the destination holds W10
6	lenr0-only-one	MAN:H7-12	LENR = 0 moves exactly one word: the next destination word still holds its sentinel
7	sid-first	MAN:H7-11	DCR SI/D set steps the source down: the first destination word is W3
8	sid-last	MAN:H7-11	DCR SI/D set: the fourth destination word is W0
9	did-first	MAN:H7-11	DCR DI/D set steps the destination down: W0 lands at the highest address
10	did-last	MAN:H7-11	DCR DI/D set: W3 lands at the lowest address
11	dv-enable-clear	ASSUMED:LED-VID-0008	With DCR bit 1 clear the end of the transfer sets no flag: the status read is $00 (the converse of H7-4, outside the page statement)
12	dv-set	MAN:H7-4	With DCR bit 1 set the end of the transfer sets DV, bit 4 of the status: $10
13	dv-read-clears	MAN:H7-4	The status read cleared DV: the next read is $00
14	iw-no-effect	ASSUMED:LED-VID-0014	IW does not apply to the transfer: with CR IW = 11 the destination is still consecutive
15	overlap-propagates	ASSUMED:LED-VID-0014	A forward overlapping copy propagates: the fifth word equals the first
16	buffer-untouched	ASSUMED:LED-VID-0014	The transfer leaves the read buffer alone
17	marr-untouched	ASSUMED:LED-VID-0014	The transfer leaves MARR alone: the next read operation loads the word MARR named
18	mawr-untouched	ASSUMED:LED-VID-0014	The transfer leaves MAWR alone: a word written afterwards lands at MAWR
19	lenr-low-alone	MAN:H7-12	The transfer is triggered by the LENR high byte: a low byte write alone starts nothing
20	lenr-high-retrigger	ASSUMED:LED-VID-0014	A lone LENR high byte write retriggers with the stored low byte
21	poll-count	ASSUMED:LED-VID-0014	The number of polls until the last destination word arrives, recorded (VL1: no speed claim; judged by no literal)	observe
22	overrun-first-word	ASSUMED:LED-VID-0014	A transfer started at the VBlank entry with SB set is cut at the display start: its first word has moved
23	overrun-last-word	ASSUMED:LED-VID-0014	The cut transfer never reached its last word
24	overrun-no-dv	ASSUMED:LED-VID-0014	A transfer cancelled by the start of a display period sets no end status (H7-4): bit 4 of the status read after the next VBlank is 0 although DV is enabled; ASSUMED because the copy still runs at the display start only under the modelled speed (ER-10)
